t its  struggling economies  it doesn't seem to care that much about  human rights in china  the chinese president spoke yesterday  and he and i  agree on that we see a need for  multilateralism  we need to find a new mode of  cooperation between states  basically to go back to an efficient  brand of multi-natural  lateralism america is back  diplomacy is back at the center of our  foreign policy  america is back ready to lead the world  well translation appeasement is upon us  and it's funny though they never seem to  hesitate  when it's time to criticize us the  voters right they have no problem  criticizing people who believe  in america first or anti-globalization  but  china no they back away how are they  going to lead the world  if it has to go hat in hand to an evil  regime like  china that's not leading that's giving  in  joe biden claims that you know america  is back and he wants to be the world  leader  well if that's really true he should  start  by announcing a boycott of the 2022  winter games in beijing  and then convince our allies in europe  and elsewhere to join the boycott  when the olympic committee let hitler  host the 1936 games in berlin  it was a dark stain on the games that  lasted for decades  it was just big propaganda a coup for  the nazis  and it's going to be the exact same for  the chinese communists  imagine president xi walking into that  stadium for the first time  lording over the crowd packed in tight  to show that the decadent west  uh boy you guys haven't overcome covid  but we have with his  air of superiority now if we're there if  the united states is there  the ccp will just argue that our  complaints about human rights they don't  really mean anything we just say that we  mow the words  that we're just too weak to resist china  that we'll always do what we're told  and many observers around the world i'm  afraid will agree  now in the past we've had presidents who  were brave enough to take on rogue  regimes  heck if jimmy carter could stand up to  the ussr in 1980  biden can stand up to the ccp today  but i'm not holding my breath for most  of his career  old joe has defended china from its  critics  and he's still doing so the idea i'm not  going to speak  out against what he's doing in hong kong  what he's doing with the uyghurs in  western  mountains of of uh china and taiwan  trying to end the one china policy by  making it forceful  he gets it culturally there are  different  norms that each country and they their  leaders are expected to follow  just different cultural norms that whole  thing they're doing with the uyghurs but  i'll mouth the words  you see what he did there now of course  establishment figures such as  mitt romney well they're pushing back on  the idea of a boycott claiming  it would punish our athletes now to be  blunt  that's just pathetic the angle of course  empathizes with athletes we love the  athletes who participate in the games  and they've trained so hard to compete  and of course the ioc the problem is  they never should have awarded the games  to china in the first place  but rewarding china after its actions  surrounding the virus  and its gross human rights abuses it's  not an  option china is desperately seeking  legitimacy on the world stage  and we should not give it to them now of  course corporate america has no problem  being associated with china  we know that from what nike's done this  is a list of u.s companies who  are top-tier sponsors for the 2020 games  it's a big one now the cato institute's  doug bandau  also disagrees with the boycott as well  he argues that  a solitary or almost solitary holdout by  the u.s  might make some feel righteous but it  would likely be counterproductive  a unitary action would highlight  america's isolation  beijing would feel emboldened more  convinced that no one was prepared to  confront  even its worst behavior well his  arguments are kind of  unpersuasive the boycott would show the  world that we're not going to treat  china as a normal country any longer  perhaps we couldn't convince  you know some of our allies to join the  boycott but they probably side with  china no matter what we did  at least we wouldn't be selling out our  own principles doesn't that count for  something  the bind administration has apparently  not made reportedly a final decision on  china again that's what they claim  but regardless of what the us government  and the international olympic committee  decide to do  we as consumers should all refuse to  watch the games  the ioc gets an enormous amount of money  for the u.s tv  rights and we need to show nbc and the  ioc that those rights  will be worthless if they insist on  acting  as a ccp promoter or a legitimizer  allowing china to become the world's  most powerful country  was a catastrophic failure of u.s policy  making  with blame from everyone from george h.w  bush  to joe biden but if we want to remain  independent ourselves we americans are  going to have to get used to the idea  of sometimes being a lonely beacon for  freedom in the world  a world dominated now by dictatorships  and technocrats  the 2022 olympics would be a good place  to start

